       <p class="card-desc">Hitler's strategic cipher. 12 rotor wheels, fully automatic teleprinter encryption. An operator's mistake in 1941 gave Bill Tutte enough to reconstruct the entire machine structure without ever seeing it. Tommy Flowers built Colossus to crack it — the world's first programmable electronic computer.</p>
