       <div class="card-name">Pigpen Cipher</div>
       <p class="card-desc">Geometric symbols derived from two grids and two X-patterns represent the 26 letters. Used by Freemasons for lodge records, appearing in gravestones, letters, and documents across three centuries. George Washington's brothers used it. It's a monoalphabetic substitution cipher — broken by frequency analysis in minutes.</p>
