       <div class="card-name">Bacon's Cipher</div>
       <p class="card-desc">Sir Francis Bacon encoded the alphabet as 5-bit binary sequences (A=AAAAA, B=AAAAB…). Used steganographically: hide messages in printed text by using two slightly different typefaces — italic for B, normal for A. Cryptographically trivial. Historically profound: this is binary encoding, described 343 years before digital computing.</p>
