       <div class="card-name">Copiale Cipher</div>
       <p class="card-desc">A 105-page bound manuscript in Roman letters, Greek letters, and abstract symbols. Sat unsolved in an East German archive for 250 years. In 2011 a USC/Uppsala team — Kevin Knight, Beata Megyesi, Christiane Schaefer — cracked it with statistical attacks borrowed from machine translation. The plaintext: initiation rites of an 18th-century German oculist secret society.</p>
